Notebook[{Cell["Partonic Born cross sections, FORM route: the same table with \
FORM and its colour library", "Title"], Cell["Same task and same output \
format as 1-Born.wl (the FeynCalc route), with FORM doing all the spin, \
Lorentz and colour algebra.  Input: the amplitude records of all 29 channels \
written by 1-Born.wl (Results/Amplitudes.wl), and its table Results/Born.wl \
for the comparison.  Output: Results/FORM/Born.wl.\n\nMathematica only writes \
the amplitudes to a file (amplitudes.inc, one local expression Amp1 ... Amp29 \
per channel), runs the FORM program form/Born.frm twice (SPIN = U, spin sum; \
SPIN = P, helicity difference of the incoming partons) and reads the squares \
back.  Open form/common.h and form/Born.frm to follow the algebra; for every \
channel the program\n\n  1. multiplies the amplitude by its complex conjugate \
(reversed gamma strings, transposed generators, primed summed indices);\n  2. \
sums over all colours with FORM's colour library color.h (#call docolor), \
before any Dirac algebra, and specializes the group invariants to SU(Nc) with \
Tr(T^a T^b) = delta^{ab}/2, the normalization of the FeynCalc route;\n  3. \
closes the fermion lines into traces with the spin sums of the quarks: one \
trace or two, depending on how the quark lines of the two interfering \
diagrams connect;\n  4. inserts the spin densities: p-slash gamma5 (-p-slash \
gamma5 for an antiquark) for a polarized incoming quark, with the HVBM gamma5 \
written through a four-dimensional epsilon tensor, gamma5 = -(i/24) eps_{mu \
nu rho sigma} gamma^mu gamma^nu gamma^rho gamma^sigma, normalized so that \
Tr[gamma^a gamma^b gamma^c gamma^d gamma5] = -4 i eps^{abcd} (FeynCalc with \
$LeviCivitaSign = -1; checked below); the circular density i eps^{mu nu l \
r}/(2 l.r) for a polarized incoming gluon l, r being the other incoming \
momentum; for every other gluon the physical polarization sum -g^{mu nu} + \
(l^mu r^nu + r^mu l^nu)/(l.r) with the reference vectors of 1-Born.wl, r = pb \
for l = pa and r = pa for l = pb, p, pd;\n  5. evaluates the D-dimensional \
traces (tracen), contracts the indices (indices inside epsilon tensors are \
four-dimensional) and inserts the kinematics s = 2 pa.pb, t = -2 pa.p, u = -2 \
pb.p.  FORM contracts two epsilon tensors with the Euclidean sign (eps_{abcd} \
eps_{abcd} = +24 instead of the Minkowski -24); every LL term contains \
exactly two of them, one per polarized incoming parton, so the LL squares are \
multiplied by -1.\n\nThe spin and colour averages of the incoming partons are \
applied here afterwards, exactly as in 1-Born.wl.  The FORM squares must \
equal the FeynCalc table exactly, for every channel, both spin cases, \
arbitrary D and arbitrary number of colours Nc.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Load and export", "Section"], Cell["Load the FeynFacet package \
(amplitude records, the FORM interface WriteFORMAmplitudes, RunFORM, \
ReadFORM, and the checks Require).", "Text"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{Noteboo\
kDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["The amplitude records of 1-Born.wl, channel by channel, are written \
to amplitudes.inc; the FORM expression Amp<i> is the amplitude of the i-th \
channel of this list, and the table shows how many records (terms with one \
colour factor and one set of fermion chains) each amplitude has.  With \
\"ColorLibrary\" -> True the colour objects are written in the conventions of \
color.h: generators T(i,j,a) = (T^a)_{ij} with the adjoint index last, \
structure constants f(a,b,c), d_ for both colour deltas, quark colours with \
dimension NR and gluon colours with dimension NA.  The declarations of all \
symbols, vectors and indices go to declarations.inc, in the same directory.", 
   "Text"], Cell["amplitudes = LoadAmplitudes[];\nchannels = \
amplitudes[\"Channels\"];\nwork = \
ResultsDirectory[\"FORM\"];\nWriteFORMAmplitudes[Association @ Table[\"Amp\" \
<> ToString[i] -> amplitudes[\"Records\"][channels[[i]]], {i, \
Length[channels]}], work, \"ColorLibrary\" -> \
True];\nTableForm[Table[{\"Amp\" <> ToString[i], channels[[i]], \
Length[amplitudes[\"Records\"][channels[[i]]]]}, {i, Length[channels]}],\n  \
TableHeadings -> {None, {\"FORM expression\", \"channel\", \"records\"}}]", 
   "Input"], Cell["As an example, the amplitude of q g -> q in FORM notation \
(three diagrams: s- and u-channel quark exchange, t-channel gluon exchange \
with the three-gluon vertex):", "Text"], Cell["First[Select[StringSplit[Impor\
t[FileNameJoin[{work, \"amplitudes.inc\"}], \"Text\"], \"L \"],\n  \
StringStartsQ[#, \"Amp\" <> ToString[First[FirstPosition[channels, \"q g -> \
q\"]]] <> \" \"] &]]", "Input"], Cell["Run the FORM program", "Section"], 
  Cell["Born.frm loops over the channels and writes the squares, in channel \
order, to BornU.m (SPIN = U) and BornP.m (SPIN = P).  It runs with TFORM, the \
multi-threaded version of FORM, on three worker threads; a FORM error stops \
the notebook.  The output shows the two result files.", "Text"], 
  Cell["program = FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"form\", \
\"Born.frm\"}];\nDo[RunFORM[program, work, \"Workers\" -> 3, \"Define\" -> \
{\"SPIN=\" <> spin, \"CHANNELS=\" <> ToString[Length[channels]]}], {spin, \
{\"U\", \"P\"}}];\nFileNames[\"Born*.m\", work]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Born.frm (SPIN = P) prints G5Check, the difference between the trace \
Tr[gamma^a gamma^b gamma^c gamma^d gamma5] computed with the explicit HVBM \
gamma5 and -4 i eps^{abcd} (FeynCalc's convention with $LeviCivitaSign = -1); \
it must vanish.", "Text"], Cell["formLog = Import[FileNameJoin[{work, \
\"Born-SPIN=P-CHANNELS=\" <> ToString[Length[channels]] <> \".log\"}], \
\"Text\"];\ng5Check = StringDelete[First[StringCases[formLog, \"G5Check =\" \
~~ Shortest[x__] ~~ \";\" :> x]], Whitespace | \"(\" | \
\")\"];\nRequire[g5Check === \"0\", \"gamma5 normalization check failed in \
Born.frm\", g5Check];\n\"G5Check = \" <> g5Check", "Input"], 
  Cell["Averages and comparison with the FeynCalc table", "Section"], 
  Cell["FORM returns |M|^2 summed over the colours of all four partons and \
over the spins (UU), or with the spin densities of the two incoming partons \
(LL), in terms of s, t, u, D, Nc and gs.  The averages are those of \
1-Born.wl: 1/(2 Nc) for an incoming quark (2 spin states times Nc colours; \
for LL the 1/2 turns p-slash gamma5 into the helicity density p-slash \
gamma5/2); 1/((D-2)(Nc^2-1)) for an unpolarized incoming gluon (D-2 \
polarization states in D dimensions), 1/(Nc^2-1) for a polarized one (its 1/2 \
is in the circular density).  The result is divided by gs^4 and written with \
u = -s-t; the output is the channel q g -> q as an example.", "Text"], 
  Cell["incoming[channel_String] := Take[StringSplit[channel], \
2];\naverage[channel_, spinCase_] := Times @@ (Switch[#, \"g\", If[spinCase \
=== \"LL\", 1, 1/(D - 2)]/(Nc^2 - 1), _, 1/(2 Nc)] & /@ \
incoming[channel]);\nformSquares = <|\"UU\" -> ReadFORM[work, \"BornU.m\"], \
\"LL\" -> ReadFORM[work, \"BornP.m\"]|>;\nRequire[Length /@ \
Values[formSquares] === {Length[channels], Length[channels]}, \"FORM did not \
return one square per channel\"];\nbornNc = Association @ Table[spinCase -> \
Association @ Table[channels[[i]] ->\n    \
Factor[Together[average[channels[[i]], spinCase] \
formSquares[spinCase][[i]]/gs^4 /. u -> -s - t]], {i, Length[channels]}], \
{spinCase, {\"UU\", \"LL\"}}];\nbornNc[\"UU\"][\"q g -> q\"]", "Input"], 
  Cell["The comparison: the FeynCalc table is written with CF and CA; with CF \
= (Nc^2-1)/(2 Nc) and CA = Nc both tables are rational functions of s, t, D \
and Nc, and their difference must vanish identically, channel by channel.", 
   "Text"], Cell["feynCalc = LoadResult[\"Born\"][\"Born\"];\ntoNc = {CF -> \
(Nc^2 - 1)/(2 Nc), CA -> Nc};\ndifference = Association @ Table[spinCase -> \
Association @ Table[channel ->\n    Together[bornNc[spinCase][channel] - \
(feynCalc[spinCase][channel] /. toNc)], {channel, channels}], {spinCase, \
{\"UU\", \"LL\"}}];\nRequire[Union[Flatten[Values /@ Values[difference]]] === \
{0}, \"The FORM table differs from the FeynCalc table\", \
difference];\nTableForm[Table[{channel, difference[\"UU\"][channel], \
difference[\"LL\"][channel]}, {channel, channels}],\n  TableHeadings -> \
{None, {\"channel\", \"UU: FORM - FeynCalc\", \"LL: FORM - FeynCalc\"}}]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Save", "Section"], Cell["Written in the format of the \
FeynCalc route: CF and CA restored as in 1-Born.wl ((Nc-1)(Nc+1) = 2 Nc CF, \
then Nc = CA).  The saved table is checked once more against the FeynCalc \
one; the output lists the saved channels.", "Text"], 
  Cell["colourFactors[expr_] := Factor[expr] /. (-1 + Nc) (1 + Nc) -> 2 Nc CF \
/. Nc -> CA;\nborn = Map[colourFactors, bornNc, \
{2}];\nRequire[Union[Flatten[Table[Together[(born[sc][ch] - feynCalc[sc][ch]) \
/. toNc], {sc, {\"UU\", \"LL\"}}, {ch, channels}]]] === {0},\n  \"The saved \
FORM table differs from the FeynCalc table\"];\nresult = <|\"Born\" -> born, \
\"Channels\" -> channels, \"Variables\" -> \"s, t (u = -s-t), D, CF, CA; \
divided by gs^4\"|>;\nSaveResult[\"Born\", result, \
\"FORM\"];\nKeys[born[\"UU\"]]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
